args: opentide --json validate query --help
exit: 0

━━━ stdout
Check rule queries offline with the analysis engine, or on the tenants (--live).

Offline, the engine reports the queries the platform would reject, as
`opentide validate` does; `opentide lint` reports their style.

Usage: opentide validate query [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --platform <PLATFORM>
          Check this platform's queries. Offline, default every platform the engine parses: sentinel, microsoft_defender, splunk, crowdstrike, harfanglab, carbon_black_cloud, elastic, sysdig, bitdefender, graylog, exabeam, google_secops, datadog. --live needs one of: sentinel, microsoft_defender, splunk, sentinel_one, carbon_black_cloud, elastic, graylog, exabeam, google_secops, datadog
          
          [possible values: sentinel, microsoft_defender, splunk, sentinel_one, crowdstrike, harfanglab, carbon_black_cloud, elastic, sysdig, bitdefender, graylog, exabeam, google_secops, datadog]

      --strategy <STRATEGY>
          Check only rules a run with this strategy deploys (repeatable), on the tenants that accept it. Default: PREVIEW and RELEASE

      --wide
          Check every status strategy but DISABLEMENT and DELETION (--live)

      --live
          Check the queries on the platform's tenants (needs credentials)

      --changed
          Check only the rule files this run changed: the pull or merge request, the push, or outside CI the last commit (the files deploy reads)

      --file <FILE>
          Check only this rule file, or this query file (.kql, .spl, .esql, .eql, .kuery, .lucene, .falco, .yar, .yara, .yaral, .yl2, .cql, .exabeam, .datadog) offline (repeatable)

      --uuid <UUID>
          Check only the rule with this UUID (repeatable)

      --strict
          Fail on warnings too

      --queries <error|warn>
          How a rejected query is reported offline: error (the default) or warn
          
          [possible values: error, warn, off]

      --check-timeout <SECONDS>
          Seconds each query may take on a tenant before its check fails (--live; default: OPENTIDE_QUERY_CHECK_TIMEOUT, else 120)

      --help
          Print help

Examples:
  $ opentide validate query
  $ opentide validate query --platform splunk --changed
  $ opentide validate query --file hunting/lsass.kql
  $ opentide validate query --platform sentinel --live

━━━ stderr · empty
